# BUG-295 — THE NEGATIVE CONTROL, and it is what makes the cycle diagnostic worth
# having. `bug295_diamond_lib_leaf` is imported by TWO different parents, so it is
# skipped on its second visit exactly like a cycle's re-entry — the skip that
# `visited` alone cannot distinguish.
#
# It must compile SILENTLY. A detector that fires here would be reporting the most
# ordinary shape in any dependency graph, and a diagnostic at that noise ratio gets
# suppressed wholesale rather than read.
use bug295_diamond_lib_left exposing leftValue
use bug295_diamond_lib_right exposing rightValue

def main()
    print("bug295-diamond=${leftValue() + rightValue()}")
